{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs36 Motion Tracking\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 There are two ways to determine when motion completes:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab {\b CommandedPositonReached} - the motion is complete when trajectory generator registers for commanded velocity and acceleration become zero (0). The {\i Settle Time} and {\i Settle Window} parameters are ignored.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab {\b AxisSettled} - the move completes once the axis reaches the commanded position and has {\i settled}. The axis is considered to be {\i settled} when the following are true: profile generator commanded motion is complete, the position error is less than the Settle Window, and both of the previous conditions have been met for the amount of time specified by Settle Time.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\pict\pngblip\picw598\pich290\picwgoal8970\pichgoal4350\bin }\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 These settings may be stored in the motion controller's NVRAM so they persist across power cycles. The axis must first be de-energized before they can be written to NVRAM. i.e.\par}
